ion/math-academy-id "q-31676" :question/problem "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨2{t}^{2}-4t,5t-{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}-4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t-{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t-4,\\,5-3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨4(2)-4,\\,5-3(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8-4,\\,5-12⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-31676/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "318d38c5-d3fb-52bf-8a88-5592f8301f89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31676"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/aaadf8d2d6216af4c8d065895fa8b4e1c6257905923832532ca2d16a4550e365" :answer/id #uuid "df6f400e-6868-5262-8b3d-81a6c3addb3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/a74318b1d4a7b6329d6cdb9309d30f677e00eed255b5399d864a2666fb6cff58" :answer/id #uuid "9226f690-8674-5c6b-a2c2-a41e1bb95297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/0081d7f4faa90b54ec79768898a23d6f03e74ff571e6715e653124906c661ee3" :answer/id #uuid "7e1a9cf8-7322-5e16-8f43-02d60f55e9fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/33abccbb767addf718fd954c8c85066179e2aa0bd7a9add3c72f943b27feb156" :answer/id #uuid "8102f1af-70e5-5036-bae4-baf5a0f4e445" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection/f0cfd8c23bdb337e809b8439f1359ea6720e934fc72fb153825d52c068a24339" :answer/id #uuid "a60c4cfe-565c-53e1-b870-793230b3ecff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9da3ca1-da5b-54f6-a305-e07a501113f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31674/selection/33abccbb767addf718fd954c8c85066179e2aa0bd7a9add3c72f943b27feb156" :answer-field/choices ["q-31674/selection/aaadf8d2d6216af4c8d065895fa8b4e1c6257905923832532ca2d16a4550e365" "q-31674/selection/a74318b1d4a7b6329d6cdb9309d30f677e00eed255b5399d864a2666fb6cff58" "q-31674/selection/0081d7f4faa90b54ec79768898a23d6f03e74ff571e6715e653124906c661ee3" "q-31674/selection/33abccbb767addf718fd954c8c85066179e2aa0bd7a9add3c72f943b27feb156" "q-31674/selection/f0cfd8c23bdb337e809b8439f1359ea6720e934fc72fb153825d52c068a24339"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31674" :question/id #uuid "02e655a7-f62a-5372-af55-721af23395e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-31674" :question/problem "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩,$ measured in $\\text{m}/\\text{s},$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}^{2}+2t,6{t}^{2}-3⟩.\n$$\n\nFind the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+2,\\,12t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨2(0)+2,12(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(0)|:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(0)| & =|⟨2,0⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(0)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31674/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "318d38c5-d3fb-52bf-8a88-5592f8301f89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31674"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347193/field-1/d167a88de8279919cd4426c42b45e96cbe79db72f579f94ad0ef2d59e0ddf3e4" :answer/id #uuid "e4e3f525-260a-55e0-9f95-79f3101b7c7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347193/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e0dc915-7e53-5e77-89bb-a2bbfb0fa057" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347193/field-1/d167a88de8279919cd4426c42b45e96cbe79db72f579f94ad0ef2d59e0ddf3e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-347193/field-1/d167a88de8279919cd4426c42b45e96cbe79db72f579f94ad0ef2d59e0ddf3e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347193/field-2/06a118dc6ea99e1c43acc826fd85a9cecda4ddb6e72af837e59ccfc9f16577e5" :answer/id #uuid "ac1ffb2d-009b-5532-a629-10e950239817" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12t^2-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347193/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "81366150-616c-5287-a8f2-dc0553180241" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347193/field-2/06a118dc6ea99e1c43acc826fd85a9cecda4ddb6e72af837e59ccfc9f16577e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-347193/field-2/06a118dc6ea99e1c43acc826fd85a9cecda4ddb6e72af837e59ccfc9f16577e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347193" :question/id #uuid "fcffff13-cdb5-5338-a8c9-56f6f641a2ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-347193" :question/problem "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-2t,\\,{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-2,\\,4{t}^{3}-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t,\\,12{t}^{2}-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-347193/field-1" "q-347193/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "380357c3-4914-5137-9449-0e02076cb248"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347193"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85606/selection/9ed0ed6f0a13f9b84ea375da7833c7f6b6c9b9630a4272e26ab0020be5a0404c" :answer/id #uuid "70743ad9-3d7e-508b-b4b6-624bca478ca7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=⟨9{t}^{2}+1,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85606/selection/a5b3eb3e3b5d3448899fd9cc8285b49663d7a1a81894fbcd5d9fbf04f64b0f07" :answer/id #uuid "d0a481d7-fb0c-51a6-964b-477a9ff77736" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=⟨18t,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85606/selection/1af83eafb319f17eaeda43a12a1d7f88d4e5370bd27b76a154d748f220f55a5c" :answer/id #uuid "b1efa112-9f29-571b-9209-166dc1d8a981" :answer/ty